+# Application Skills Overview
+
+This document provides an overview of the Reliability AI Agent's capabilities, organized by domain. Each skill is documented in detail in the `skills/` directory.
+
+## Skills Documentation
+
+- `SKILLS_INDEX.md` provides an overview of available application skills and their relationships.
+- Consult the relevant detailed skill documents under `skills/` before modifying their functionality.
+- Treat skill documentation as a technical reference.
+- Verify documented capabilities against the actual implementation and tests.
+- Update relevant skill documentation when functionality or tool contracts change.
+
+## Skill Organization
+
+Skills are organized into four areas:
+
+1. **Reliability Domain** - Reliability engineering calculations and analysis
+2. **MCP Integration** - Model Context Protocol tool integration
+3. **Knowledge Base** - Document ingestion and hybrid RAG search
+4. **UI Interaction** - Frontend chat interface and user interaction
+
+## Reliability Domain Skills
+
+### Weibull Analysis
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/weibull-analysis.md`
+
+Fits 2-parameter Weibull distribution to failure times with right-censored suspensions. Generates probability paper plots with Bernard/Herd-Johnson median ranks. Supports RRY (Rank Regression on Y) and MLE (Maximum Likelihood Estimation) methods with optional bootstrap confidence intervals.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Failure time analysis with censored/suspended data
+- Median rank calculation (Bernard's approximation)
+- RRY method (default) or MLE
+- Bootstrap percentile bounds on fitted line and B-life
+- Probability paper plot generation (matplotlib)
+- β (shape) and η (scale) parameter estimation
+- MTBF calculation from fitted parameters
+
+**MCP Tool**: `analyze_weibull`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/weibull.py`
+**Core Math**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/weibull_fit.py` (calculation), `backend/src/domains/reliability/plotting.py` (paper)
+
+### B-Life Calculation
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/b-life-calculation.md`
+
+Calculates Weibull B-life (time at which a given percentage of units have failed) from fitted β and η parameters. Commonly used for B10, B20, B30 in warranty analysis.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Computes time-to-failure for any percentile (0-100%)
+- Uses Weibull cumulative distribution function
+- Returns integer hours
+- Used for warranty coverage analysis
+
+**MCP Tool**: `calculate_b_life`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/blife.py`
+**Core Math**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/weibull_fit.py`
+
+### MTBF Calculation
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/mtbf-calculation.md`
+
+Calculates Mean Time Between Failures from failure times and optionally censored times. Provided as a plugin example demonstrating the plugin system.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Total operating time calculation
+- Failure rate computation
+- MTBF = total time / failures
+- Handles censored/suspended units
+- Plugin-based extensibility
+
+### Reliability Growth
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/reliability-growth.md`
+
+Duane + Crow-AMSAA / Power-Law NHPP growth analysis for a single repairable system. Fits Duane log-log cumulative MTBF (α, R²) and Crow-AMSAA MLE (β, λ, intensity, instantaneous MTBF, CvM GOF), with forecast of future MTBF. Failure- or time-terminated.
+
+**MCP Tools**: `analyze_reliability_growth`, `forecast_growth_mtbf`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/growth_fit.py`, `growth_plot.py`, `tools/growth.py`
+
+**MCP Tool**: `calculate_mtbf` (plugin)
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/plugins/mtbf.py`
+
+### Warranty Forecast & Demonstration-Test Planning
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/warranty-planning.md`
+
+Forecasts field failures within a warranty period and plans zero-failure demonstration tests. Both are deterministic and assumption-explicit; missing population/duration/target inputs must be asked for, never assumed.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Warranty forecast: Weibull CDF at warranty time + Binomial(population, F) expectation and central interval
+- Demonstration plan: success-run relation `C = 1 - R^(n*(t/mission_time)^beta)`, solving sample size or test duration
+- States independence/exposure assumptions and that fit uncertainty is not propagated into the forecast interval
+
+**MCP Tools**: `forecast_warranty_failures`, `plan_demonstration_test`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/planning.py`
+**Core Math**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/planning.py`
+
+### Knowledge Search
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/knowledge-search.md`
+
+Hybrid search over reliability engineering documents (handbooks, procedures, notes). Combines vector similarity (ChromaDB) with BM25 keyword matching for comprehensive retrieval.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Hybrid retrieval (vector + BM25)
+- Document citation with source and chunk number
+- Searches local knowledge-base directory
+- Supports multiple document formats (.md, .txt, .pdf, .docx, .pptx)
+- Configurable max results
+- Cites sources in LLM responses
+
+**MCP Tool**: `search_reliability_knowledge`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/knowledge_tool.py`
+**Core RAG**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+
+### Report Generation
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/report-generation.md`
+
+Generates a one-page markdown report summarizing Weibull analysis with optional warranty comparison and knowledge base citations. Creates defensible documentation for design reviews.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- One-page markdown format
+- Includes β, η, sample size, method
+- Compares B10/B20/B30 to warranty period
+- Cites knowledge base sources
+- Embeds plot filename
+- Saves to `backend/static/reliability_report.md`
+- Table data matches plot
+
+**MCP Tool**: `export_reliability_report`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/report.py`
+**Report Template**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/reliability_report.py`
+
+### Distribution Analysis
+
+KM empirical reference, AIC distribution ranking, single-commit or multi-compare shortlist, and censored fits. Prescribes computations; never invents metrics.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- KM empirical reference with Greenwood bounds and hazard cue
+- AIC ranking across candidate families
+- Single-commit or multi-compare shortlist
+- One censored-MLE engine for all families
+- Numeric questions routed to compute tools
+
+**MCP Tools**: `analyze_nonparametric_life_data`, `fit_life_distribution`, `select_life_distribution`, `analyze_exploratory_data`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/nonparametric.py`, `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/distributions.py`
+**Calculation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/nonparametric.py` (Kaplan-Meier), `backend/src/domains/reliability/distributions.py` (one censored-MLE engine for exponential, Weibull, normal, lognormal, logistic, loglogistic, Gumbel/SEV), `backend/src/domains/reliability/eda.py` (NIST 4-plot statistics)
+
+### Exploratory Data Analysis
+
+**File**: `skills/reliability-domain/eda-plots.md`
+
+NIST 4-plot EDA (run sequence, lag-1, histogram, normal probability) with summary statistics, run before any distribution is assumed.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Lag-1 autocorrelation for randomness checks
+- Normal-paper correlation for shape checks
+- Small-sample warning below 30 values
+- 4-panel PNG for design reviews
+
+**MCP Tool**: `analyze_exploratory_data`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/eda.py`
+
+## MCP Integration Skills
+
+### MCP Tools
+**File**: `skills/mcp-integration/mcp-tools.md`
+
+Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool registration and execution system. Bridges LLM agents to computational tools via stdio or HTTP transport.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Tool registration with `@mcp.tool()` decorator
+- Automatic tool discovery and listing
+- Argument validation via Pydantic
+- JSON serialization of results
+- Image block support for plots
+- Multi-transport support (stdio, SSE, streamable HTTP)
+- LlamaIndex FunctionTool conversion
+
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/host/mcp_pool.py` (MultiMCPClient)
+**Domain Servers**: `backend/src/domains/*/server.py`
+
+## Knowledge Base Skills
+
+### Document Ingestion
+**File**: `skills/knowledge-base/document-ingestion.md`
+
+Processes and indexes documents for hybrid RAG search. Supports multiple formats with local parsing using Docling.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Supported formats: .md, .txt, .pdf, .doc, .docx, .ppt, .pptx
+- Local parsing with Docling (no cloud dependency)
+- Paragraph-level chunking with overlap
+- Metadata extraction (page numbers, sections)
+- Incremental indexing (only changed files)
+- File change detection via SHA256
+- Sentence Transformers embeddings (local)
+
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py` (GenericKnowledgeBase)
+**Parsing**: Docling library for PDF/Office documents
+**Embeddings**: Sentence Transformers (EMBEDDING_MODEL env var)
+
+### Hybrid RAG
+**File**: `skills/knowledge-base/hybrid-rag.md`
+
+Hybrid retrieval combining vector similarity search (ChromaDB) with BM25 keyword matching. Provides comprehensive document retrieval for knowledge queries.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Vector similarity (semantic search)
+- BM25 keyword matching (exact terms)
+- Score fusion (weighted combination)
+- Single collection (`reliability_knowledge`)
+- Configurable max results
+- Source citation with metadata
+- Local embeddings (no API calls)
+
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+**Vector DB**: ChromaDB
+**Keyword Search**: rank-bm25
+**Embeddings**: Sentence Transformers
+
+## UI Interaction Skills
+
+### Chat Interface
+**File**: `skills/ui-interaction/chat-interface.md`
+
+React-based chat interface with Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming for real-time LLM responses. Supports multi-session management and message actions.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- SSE streaming (token, thought, tool events)
+- Multi-session history with localStorage
+- Message search across sessions
+- Per-message actions (copy, edit, regenerate, delete)
+- Foldable thinking panel
+- Image rendering for plots
+- Message timestamps and model labels
+- Response statistics (time, tokens)
+- Stop generation button
+- Markdown export (Markdown/HTML/PDF)
+
+**Implementation**: `frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/MessageItem.tsx`
+**Streaming**: `frontend/src/services/http.ts` (streamSse)
+**Session Management**: `frontend/src/hooks/useSessions.ts`
+
+### Model Picker
+**File**: `skills/ui-interaction/model-picker.md`
+
+LLM provider selection and configuration interface supporting multiple OpenAI-compatible endpoints.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Provider presets (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp, Unsloth, LiteRT-LM, OpenAI, custom)
+- Base URL configuration with normalization
+- API key input (write-only, not persisted in localStorage)
+- Model selection from `/api/models` endpoint
+- Manual model ID entry
+- Connection testing
+- Model refresh button
+- Provider badge in chat
+
+**Implementation**: `frontend/src/components/ModelPicker.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`
+**API**: `GET /api/models`, `POST /api/llm/test`
+**Backend**: `backend/src/host/app.py` (provider resolution, model listing)
+
+### Settings Panel
+**File**: `skills/ui-interaction/settings-panel.md`
+
+Configuration panel for LLM settings, MCP tool inventory, and app preferences. Persists non-sensitive settings to backend.
+
+**Key Features**:
+- LLM configuration (provider, base URL, model, temperature, system prompt)
+- Knowledge base status display
+- MCP tool inventory (names + descriptions)
+- Theme selection (system/light/dark)
+- Export format selection (Markdown/HTML/PDF)
+- Clear all chats with confirmation
+- Settings persistence to backend
+- API key management (encrypted at rest)
+
+**Implementation**: `frontend/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`
+**API**: `GET/PUT /api/llm/config`, `GET /api/knowledge/status`, `GET /api/mcp/tools`
+**Backend**: `backend/src/host/app.py` (config endpoints), `backend/src/common/credential_store.py`
+
+## Skill Interactions
+
+### Typical Reliability Workflow
+
+1. User asks: "Fit Weibull to failures 150, 180, 220, 310 with suspensions 800, 800. Does B10 cover 200h warranty?"
+2. LLM calls `analyze_weibull` tool with failure times and censored times
+3. Python computes β, η, generates plot, returns results
+4. LLM calls `calculate_b_life` with β, η, percentage=10
+5. LLM calls `search_reliability_knowledge` for warranty procedures
+6. LLM synthesizes answer with plot reference, B10 value, and citations
+7. UI streams thinking, tool calls, and final answer
+8. User can regenerate, edit, or export the conversation
+
+## Skill Dependencies
+
+### Backend Dependencies
+
+- **MCP Tools** depend on: MCP SDK, domain server, tool implementations
+- **Weibull Analysis** depends on: NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib
+- **Knowledge Base** depends on: ChromaDB, rank-bm25, Docling, Sentence Transformers
+- **Report Generation** depends on: Weibull Analysis, Knowledge Search
+
+### Frontend Dependencies
+
+- **Chat Interface** depends on: Backend SSE API, service layer
+- **Model Picker** depends on: Backend models API, provider presets
+- **Settings Panel** depends on: Backend config API, knowledge status API
+
+## Skill Configuration
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+- `EMBEDDING_MODEL` - Local embedding model for knowledge base
+- `EMBEDDING_LOCAL_FILES_ONLY` - Skip model download if true
+- `KNOWLEDGE_BASE_DIR` - Documents directory (default: `knowledge-base/`)
+
+### MCP Server Configuration
+
+- `MCP_SERVERS_CONFIG` - Override MCP server list JSON
+- `MCP_TRANSPORT` - stdio, sse, or streamable-http
+- `MCP_HOST` - MCP server bind address
+- `MCP_PORT` - MCP server port
+
+### Knowledge Base Configuration
+
+- Single collection: `reliability_knowledge`
+- Single knowledge directory: `knowledge-base/`
+- Single index directory: `backend/.rag/`
+
+## Skill Extension
+
+### Adding a New Skill
+
+1. **Backend Tool**: Create implementation in `backend/src/domains/<domain>/tools/`
+2. **Register Tool**: Add `@mcp.tool()` decorator in `server.py`
+3. **Update Prompt**: Add guidance in `prompt.md` if needed
+4. **Document Skill**: Create markdown file in `docs-spec/skills/<domain>/`
+5. **Test**: Add test in `backend/tests/`
+
+## Skill Performance
+
+### Reliability Calculations
+
+- Weibull fit: < 1 second for < 1000 data points
+- B-life calculation: < 10ms
+- MTBF calculation: < 10ms
+- Report generation: < 2 seconds (including plot)
+
+### Knowledge Base
+
+- Document ingestion: ~1-5 seconds per document (depends on size)
+- Embedding generation: ~100-500ms per chunk
+- Hybrid search: < 500ms
+- Index rebuild: Depends on document count
+
+### MCP Tool Execution
+
+- stdio transport: < 10ms tool call overhead
+- HTTP transport: < 50ms tool call overhead
+- Tool execution: Depends on computation (usually < 1 second)
+
+## Skill Limitations
+
+### Reliability Domain
+
+- Only 2-parameter Weibull (no 3-parameter or mixed Weibull)
+- No interval censoring (only right-censored suspensions)
+- Bootstrap bounds approximate (not exact)
+- Plot generation requires matplotlib backend
+
+### Knowledge Base
+
+- Local embeddings only (no cloud vector DB)
+- Document size limited by available memory
+- Incremental indexing requires file change detection
+- No document versioning
+
+### UI
+
+- No multi-user collaboration
+- No real-time updates across sessions
+- Limited export formats (Markdown/HTML/PDF via browser print)
+- No offline mode (requires backend connection)
+
+## Future Skill Enhancements
+
+### Reliability Domain
+
+- 3-parameter Weibull support
+- Interval censoring
+- Competing risk models
+- Mixed Weibull and competing-risk compound models
+- Bayesian prior integration for small samples
+
+### Knowledge Base
+
+- Cloud vector DB support (Azure Cosmos DB, Pinecone)
+- Document versioning
+- Real-time indexing (watchdog)
+- OCR for scanned PDFs
+- Table extraction
+
+### UI
+
+- Multi-user collaboration
+- Real-time session sharing
+- Direct plot download
+- LaTeX editor
+- Comparison mode (multiple analyses side-by-side)
