index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e608fb7cd153ecc7949de511acbaf725e1902ae7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/knowledge-base/document-ingestion.md
@@ -0,0 +1,352 @@
+# Document Ingestion Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Processes and indexes documents for hybrid RAG search. Supports multiple formats (.md, .txt, .pdf, .doc, .docx, .ppt, .pptx) with local parsing using Docling. Documents are chunked, embedded, and stored in ChromaDB with BM25 keyword index.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Document ingestion enables:
+
+- **Knowledge base creation**: Build searchable document collections
+- **Local processing**: All parsing happens locally (no cloud dependency)
+- **Multi-format support**: Handle various document types
+- **Incremental updates**: Only reprocess changed documents
+- **Hybrid search**: Enable both vector and keyword search
+
+## Supported Formats
+
+### Text Formats
+- **Markdown (.md)**: Technical documentation, procedures
+- **Text (.txt)**: Plain text notes
+
+### Office Formats (via Docling)
+- **PDF (.pdf)**: Handbooks, standards, reports
+- **Word (.doc, .docx)**: Procedures, specifications
+- **PowerPoint (.ppt, .pptx)**: Presentations, training materials
+
+## Implementation
+
+### Knowledge Base Class
+**File**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+
+Key classes:
+- `GenericKnowledgeBase`: Main class for document ingestion and search
+- `KnowledgeChunk`: Dataclass for text chunks with metadata
+
+### Document Pipeline
+
+```
+Document Files
+    ↓
+File Detection (scan directory)
+    ↓
+Change Detection (SHA256 hash)
+    ↓
+Docling Parsing (local)
+    ↓
+Text Extraction
+    ↓
+Chunking (paragraph-level)
+    ↓
+Embedding Generation (Sentence Transformers)
+    ↓
+ChromaDB Storage (vector embeddings)
+    ↓
+BM25 Index (keyword search)
+```
+
+### Chunking Strategy
+
+**Parameters**:
+- `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS`: 384 tokens per chunk
+- `DEFAULT_OVERLAP_TOKENS`: 64 tokens overlap
+- `default_token_count()`: Word-based token counting
+
+**Algorithm**:
+1. Split text at paragraph boundaries (double newlines)
+2. Accumulate paragraphs until token limit reached
+3. Add overlap to next chunk
+4. Repeat until all text processed
+
+### Metadata Extraction
+
+Each chunk includes:
+- `source`: Document filename
+- `chunk_number`: Chunk index in document
+- `page`: Page number (if available from Docling)
+- `section`: Section title (if available)
+- `content_type`: Document type (text, pdf, docx, etc.)
+
+## Building the Index
+
+### Command
+
+From the backend directory:
+```bash
+uv run python -m src.knowledge.base
+```
+
+### Process
+
+1. **Scan directory**: Recursively scan knowledge-base directory
+2. **Detect changes**: Compare SHA256 hashes with manifest
+3. **Process new/changed files**:
+   - Parse with Docling (PDF/Office) or read text (MD/TXT)
+   - Chunk text
+   - Generate embeddings
+   - Store in ChromaDB
+   - Update BM25 index
+4. **Remove deleted files**: Delete from ChromaDB and BM25 index
+5. **Update manifest**: Save file hashes to `backend/.rag/manifest.json`
+
+### Downloading Embedding Model
+
+First-time setup:
+```bash
+uv run python -m src.knowledge.base --download-model
+```
+
+Or set `EMBEDDING_LOCAL_FILES_ONLY=true` in `.env` to skip download if model is already cached.
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+- `EMBEDDING_MODEL`: Sentence Transformers model (default: `google/embeddinggemma-2`, text-only encoders, chunk budget 512; `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` opts back into the 256-token budget)
+- `EMBEDDING_LOCAL_FILES_ONLY`: Skip model download if true
+- `EMBEDDING_DEVICE`: cpu or cuda (default: cpu)
+
+## Knowledge Base Configuration
+
+The single reliability knowledge base (`backend/src/knowledge/base.py`):
+
+```yaml
+collection: reliability_knowledge
+knowledge_dir: knowledge-base
+index_dir: .rag
+```
+
+### Knowledge Base Paths
+
+- **Reliability**: `knowledge-base/` → `backend/.rag/`
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Basic Indexing
+
+**Scenario**: Add documents to reliability knowledge base
+
+**Steps**:
+1. Drop files into `knowledge-base/` directory
+2. Run: `uv run python -m src.knowledge.base`
+3. Output:
+```
+Processing weibull-procedures.md... 45 chunks
+Processing reliability-handbook.pdf... 128 chunks
+Processing design-standards.docx... 67 chunks
+Total: 240 chunks in collection 'reliability_knowledge'
+```
+
+### Incremental Update
+
+**Scenario**: Add new document without reprocessing existing
+
+**Steps**:
+1. Add `new-procedure.md` to `knowledge-base/`
+2. Run: `uv run python -m src.knowledge.base`
+3. Output:
+```
+Processing new-procedure.md... 23 chunks
+Skipping weibull-procedures.md (unchanged)
+Skipping reliability-handbook.pdf (unchanged)
+Skipping design-standards.docx (unchanged)
+Total: 263 chunks in collection 'reliability_knowledge'
+```
+
+### Force Rebuild
+
+**Scenario**: Force full rebuild (ignoring change detection)
+
+**Steps**:
+1. Delete `backend/.rag/` directory
+2. Run: `uv run python -m src.knowledge.base`
+3. All documents reprocessed
+
+### Indexing
+
+**Scenario**: Index the reliability knowledge base
+
+**Steps**:
+1. Add documents to `knowledge-base/`
+2. Run: `uv run python -m src.knowledge.base`
+3. Index created in `backend/.rag/`
+
+## Chat Upload
+
+### Upload via UI
+
+Users can upload documents directly in the chat interface:
+
+**Process**:
+1. User attaches file in chat composer
+2. Frontend uploads via `POST /api/knowledge/upload`
+3. Backend processes document immediately
+4. Document added to knowledge base
+5. Available for search in current and future queries
+
+**API**:
+```http
+POST /api/knowledge/upload
+Content-Type: multipart/form-data
+
+file: <binary>
+```
+
+**Response**:
+```json
+{
+  "source": "uploaded-document.pdf",
+  "indexed": true,
+  "message": "Document indexed successfully (45 chunks)"
+}
+```
+
+## Performance Characteristics
+
+### Indexing Performance
+
+- **Small documents** (< 10 pages): ~1-2 seconds
+- **Medium documents** (10-50 pages): ~5-10 seconds
+- **Large documents** (50-200 pages): ~20-60 seconds
+- **Embedding generation**: ~100-500ms per chunk
+
+### Factors Affecting Performance
+
+- **Document size**: Larger documents take longer
+- **Embedding model**: Larger models slower but more accurate
+- **CPU vs GPU**: GPU much faster for embeddings
+- **Chunk size**: Smaller chunks = more chunks = slower
+- **Number of documents**: Linear scaling
+
+### Storage Requirements
+
+- **ChromaDB**: ~1KB per chunk (embeddings + metadata)
+- **BM25 index**: ~100 bytes per chunk
+- **Manifest**: ~100 bytes per file
+- **Example**: 1000 chunks ≈ 1.1MB index size
+
+## Limitations
+
+1. **Local only**: No cloud vector DB support (currently)
+2. **File size limit**: Limited by available memory
+3. **No versioning**: No document version tracking
+4. **No OCR**: Scanned PDFs not supported (need text layer)
+5. **No table extraction**: Tables flattened to text
+6. **No real-time updates**: Must rebuild index manually
+7. **Embedding quality**: Depends on model (all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is small but fast)
+
+## Best Practices
+
+### Document Organization
+
+1. **Clear filenames**: Use descriptive names (e.g., `weibull-procedures.md`)
+2. **Logical structure**: Organize by topic in subdirectories
+3. **Consistent formatting**: Use consistent headings and structure
+4. **Avoid very long documents**: Split into smaller files (< 200 pages)
+5. **Include metadata**: Add title, author, date in document
+
+### Index Management
+
+1. **Rebuild after changes**: Run indexing after adding/modifying documents
+2. **Monitor size**: Check `backend/.rag/` directory size
+3. **Backup knowledge base**: Keep backup of `knowledge-base/` directory
+4. **Use incremental updates**: Don't force rebuild unless necessary
+5. **Test after indexing**: Verify search returns expected results
+
+### Document Quality
+
+1. **Clean text**: Remove formatting artifacts
+2. **Use headings**: Add section headers for better chunking
+3. **Consistent terminology**: Use standard terminology
+4. **Avoid duplicates**: Don't index duplicate content
+5. **Proofread**: Fix typos before indexing
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Indexing Fails
+
+**Symptoms**: Error during indexing, partial index
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Check document format is supported
+2. Verify document is not corrupted
+3. Check available memory
+4. Try processing one document at a time
+5. Check Docling installation
+
+### Search Returns No Results
+
+**Symptoms**: Search returns empty matches
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Verify index was built successfully
+2. Check collection name matches domain
+3. Verify query terms exist in documents
+4. Try different query terms
+5. Check embedding model loaded correctly
+
+### Slow Indexing
+
+**Symptoms**: Indexing takes very long
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Use GPU for embeddings (`EMBEDDING_DEVICE=cuda`)
+2. Reduce chunk size (smaller chunks = fewer tokens)
+3. Use smaller embedding model
+4. Process documents in batches
+5. Check CPU usage (other processes may be competing)
+
+### Memory Issues
+
+**Symptoms**: Out of memory errors during indexing
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Process fewer documents at a time
+2. Use smaller embedding model
+3. Increase chunk size (fewer chunks)
+4. Close other applications
+5. Add more RAM to system
+
+## Security and Privacy
+
+### Local-First Design
+
+- All processing happens locally
+- Documents never leave user's machine
+- No API calls to cloud services
+- Embeddings generated with local model
+- Vector database stored on disk
+
+### Access Control
+
+- Knowledge base access via API only
+- No direct file access from frontend
+- Optional APP_TOKEN for network deployments
+- Per-user knowledge bases in multi-user mode
+
+## Related Skills
+
+- **Knowledge Search**: Hybrid search over indexed documents
+- **Report Generation**: Can include knowledge citations in reports
+
+## References
+
+- Docling: https://github.com/DS4SD/docling
+- Sentence Transformers: https://www.sbert.net/
+- ChromaDB: https://www.trychroma.com/
+- rank-bm25: https://github.com/dorianbrown/rank_bm25
+
+## Related Files
+
+- Knowledge Base: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+- Knowledge Base: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py` (`reliability_knowledge` collection)
+- Docling Integration: Automatic via sentence-transformers
