+# Hybrid RAG Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Hybrid retrieval combining vector similarity search (ChromaDB) with BM25 keyword matching. Provides comprehensive document retrieval for knowledge queries by leveraging both semantic understanding and exact keyword matching.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Hybrid RAG enables:
+
+- **Semantic search**: Find documents by meaning, not just keywords
+- **Keyword search**: Find exact terms and phrases
+- **Comprehensive retrieval**: Combine both approaches for better results
+- **Score fusion**: Weighted combination of vector and BM25 scores
+- **Source citation**: Provide traceable references in responses
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Search Pipeline
+
+```
+User Query
+    ↓
+Query Tokenization (BM25)
+    ↓
+Query Embedding (Sentence Transformers)
+    ↓
+Vector Search (ChromaDB similarity)
+    ↓
+BM25 Search (keyword matching)
+    ↓
+Score Fusion (weighted combination)
+    ↓
+Top-K Results
+    ↓
+Return with citations
+```
+
+### Vector Search
+
+**Purpose**: Find semantically similar documents
+
+**Process**:
+1. Embed query using Sentence Transformers
+2. Query ChromaDB for nearest neighbors
+3. Return top-K results with similarity scores
+
+**Embedding Model**: `google/embeddinggemma-2` (default, local, text-only encoders) or `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (smaller, 256-token window — requires sentence-transformers ≥ 6.1 for Gemma)
+
+**ChromaDB**: Local vector database (no cloud dependency)
+
+### BM25 Search
+
+**Purpose**: Find documents with exact keyword matches
+
+**Process**:
+1. Tokenize query (lowercase, alphanumeric tokens)
+2. Query BM25 index for matching documents
+3. Return top-K results with BM25 scores
+
+**Tokenization**: Alphanumeric tokens, length > 2
+
+**Index**: In-memory rank-bm25 index
+
+### Score Fusion
+
+**Formula**:
+```
+combined_score = w_vector * vector_score + w_bm25 * bm25_score
+```
+
+**Weights**:
+- `w_vector`: 0.7 (semantic search)
+- `w_bm25`: 0.3 (keyword search)
+
+**Rationale**: Semantic search is generally more effective for natural language queries, but keyword search captures exact terms that may be missed by embeddings.
+
+## Implementation
+
+### Knowledge Base Class
+**File**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+
+Key methods:
+- `search(query, max_results)`: Hybrid search
+- `_vector_search(query_embedding, k)`: ChromaDB similarity search
+- `_bm25_search(query_tokens, k)`: BM25 keyword search
+- `_fuse_scores(vector_results, bm25_results)`: Score fusion
+
+### Vector Search
+
+```python
+def _vector_search(self, query_embedding: np.ndarray, k: int) -> list[tuple[float, str, int]]:
+    """Search ChromaDB for similar chunks."""
+    results = self.collection.query(
+        query_embeddings=[query_embedding],
+        n_results=k
+    )
+    # Return list of (score, source, chunk_number)
+```
+
+### BM25 Search
+
+```python
+def _bm25_search(self, query_tokens: list[str], k: int) -> list[tuple[float, str, int]]:
+    """Search BM25 index for matching chunks."""
+    results = self.bm25.get_scores(query_tokens)
+    # Return top-k (score, source, chunk_number)
+```
+
+### Score Fusion
+
+```python
+def _fuse_scores(
+    self,
+    vector_results: list[tuple[float, str, int]],
+    bm25_results: list[tuple[float, str, int]]
+) -> list[tuple[float, str, int]]:
+    """Combine vector and BM25 scores."""
+    # Normalize scores
+    # Apply weights
+    # Sort by combined score
+    # Return top-k
+```
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Semantic Search
+
+**Query**: "How to handle censored data in Weibull analysis?"
+
+**Vector Search**:
+- Finds documents about "censored data", "suspensions", "right-censoring"
+- Semantic match even if exact words differ
+
+**BM25 Search**:
+- Finds documents with exact words "censored", "data", "Weibull"
+
+**Combined**: Returns best matches from both approaches
+
+### Keyword Search
+
+**Query**: "Bernard median rank formula"
+
+**Vector Search**:
+- May miss if documents use different phrasing
+
+**BM25 Search**:
+- Finds documents with exact words "Bernard", "median", "rank", "formula"
+
+**Combined**: Prioritizes exact keyword matches while still considering semantic similarity
+
+### Mixed Query
+
+**Query**: "What is the procedure for calculating B10 from Weibull parameters?"
+
+**Vector Search**:
+- Finds documents about B10, Weibull, calculations, procedures
+
+**BM25 Search**:
+- Finds documents with exact words "B10", "Weibull", "parameters"
+
+**Combined**: Comprehensive results
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Embedding Model
+
+**Default**: `google/embeddinggemma-2` (text-only encoders)
+
+**Alternatives**:
+- `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`: Small and fast, 256-token window (chunk budget drops to 208)
+- `all-mpnet-base-v2`: More accurate, slower
+- `paraphrase-MiniLM-L6-v2`: Good for paraphrases
+- Custom models: Any Sentence Transformers model
+
+**Environment Variable**:
+```bash
+EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
+```
+
+### Chunking Parameters
+
+**Default**:
+- `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS`: 384 tokens per chunk
+- `DEFAULT_OVERLAP_TOKENS`: 64 tokens overlap
+
+**Customization**: Modify in `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+
+### Fusion Weights
+
+**Default**:
+- Vector weight: 0.7
+- BM25 weight: 0.3
+
+**Customization**: Modify `_fuse_scores()` method
+
+## Performance Characteristics
+
+### Search Performance
+
+- **Vector search**: < 100ms for < 10,000 chunks
+- **BM25 search**: < 50ms
+- **Combined query**: < 200ms total
+- **Scales linearly** with chunk count
+
+### Factors Affecting Performance
+
+- **Chunk count**: More chunks = slower search
+- **Embedding model**: Larger models slower
+- **CPU vs GPU**: GPU much faster for embeddings
+- **k value**: Larger k = more results = slower
+
+### Scalability
+
+- **Small KB** (< 1000 chunks): < 50ms
+- **Medium KB** (1000-10000 chunks): < 200ms
+- **Large KB** (10000-100000 chunks): < 1s
+- **Very large KB** (> 100000 chunks): Consider cloud vector DB
+
+## Limitations
+
+1. **Local only**: No cloud vector DB support (currently)
+2. **Embedding quality**: Depends on model (small models less accurate)
+3. **Fixed weights**: Fusion weights not dynamically adjusted
+4. **No reranking**: No cross-encoder reranking
+5. **No query expansion**: No automatic query expansion
+6. **No filtering**: No metadata-based filtering (yet)
+
+## Best Practices
+
+### Query Formulation
+
+1. **Use natural language**: Write queries as questions
+2. **Include specific terms**: Add technical terms for BM25
+3. **Be specific**: More specific queries = better results
+4. **Use full sentences**: Better for semantic understanding
+5. **Try variations**: If results poor, rephrase query
+
+### Knowledge Base Organization
+
+1. **Chunk size**: 384 tokens is good balance
+2. **Overlap**: 64 tokens ensures context preserved
+3. **Structure**: Use headings for better chunking
+4. **Terminology**: Use consistent terms throughout
+5. **Quality**: Proofread documents before indexing
+
+### Fusion Weights
+
+1. **Default (0.7/0.3)**: Good for most use cases
+2. **Keyword-heavy (0.5/0.5)**: For technical queries with exact terms
+3. **Semantic-heavy (0.9/0.1)**: For conceptual queries
+4. **Experiment**: Test different weights for your use case
+
+## Comparison: Vector vs BM25 vs Hybrid
+
+| Aspect | Vector Search | BM25 Search | Hybrid Search |
+|--------|--------------|-------------|---------------|
+| Semantic understanding | Excellent | Poor | Excellent |
+| Exact keyword matching | Poor | Excellent | Good |
+| Query flexibility | High | Low | High |
+| Recall | High | Medium | High |
+| Precision | Medium | High | High |
+| Best for | Conceptual queries | Technical terms | General use |
+
+## Integration with LLM
+
+### RAG Pipeline
+
+1. **User query**: "How to calculate B10?"
+2. **Knowledge search**: Hybrid search returns relevant chunks
+3. **Context injection**: Chunks added to LLM context
+4. **LLM response**: Answer with citations
+5. **Source attribution**: Each fact cites its source
+
+### Prompt Integration
+
+The system prompt instructs the LLM:
+```
+When local knowledge-base context is provided with the question, use it and cite its source.
+```
+
+This ensures:
+- LLM uses provided context
+- Sources are cited in responses
+- No hallucination from documents
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Poor Search Results
+
+**Symptoms**: Search returns irrelevant or no results
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Check index was built successfully
+2. Verify query terms exist in documents
+3. Try different query phrasing
+4. Check embedding model loaded correctly
+5. Adjust fusion weights
+
+### Slow Search
+
+**Symptoms**: Search takes very long
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Reduce chunk count (smaller documents)
+2. Use GPU for embeddings
+3. Reduce k value (fewer results)
+4. Use smaller embedding model
+5. Consider cloud vector DB for very large KB
+
+### No Vector Results
+
+**Symptoms**: Only BM25 results returned
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Check ChromaDB collection exists
+2. Verify embeddings were generated
+3. Check query embedding generation
+4. Ensure vector search is enabled
+5. Check for ChromaDB errors
+
+### No BM25 Results
+
+**Symptoms**: Only vector results returned
+
+**Solutions**:
+1. Check BM25 index was built
+2. Verify tokenization is working
+3. Check query tokens are generated
+4. Ensure BM25 search is enabled
+5. Check for rank-bm25 errors
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+### Cloud Vector DB
+
+Support for cloud vector databases:
+- Azure Cosmos DB
+- Pinecone
+- Weaviate
+- Qdrant
+
+### Reranking
+
+Cross-encoder reranking for better precision:
+- Train cross-encoder on domain data
+- Rerank top-K results
+- Improve precision
+
+### Query Expansion
+
+Automatic query expansion:
+- Synonym expansion
+- Related terms
+- Multi-query fusion
+
+### Metadata Filtering
+
+Filter results by metadata:
+- Document type
+- Date range
+- Author
+- Category
+
+## Related Skills
+
+- **Document Ingestion**: Prepares documents for search
+- **Knowledge Search**: API wrapper for hybrid search
+
+## References
+
+- Sentence Transformers: https://www.sbert.net/
+- ChromaDB: https://www.trychroma.com/
+- rank-bm25: https://github.com/dorianbrown/rank_bm25
+- RAG Best Practices: https://www.llamaindex.ai/
+
+## Related Files
+
+- Knowledge Base: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+- Domain Knowledge Tools: `backend/src/domains/*/tools/knowledge_tool.py`
