+# EDA 4-Plot Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Exploratory data analysis before modeling, following NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook
+§1.2.4 (Interpretation of 4-Plot) and §1.3.3 (graphical techniques). One tool
+call produces the classic 4-panel figure — run sequence, lag-1, histogram,
+normal probability plot — plus the summary statistics needed to read it.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Life-data and measurement data must be explored before a distribution is
+assumed. The 4-plot answers, in order: is there trend or drift (run
+sequence)? Is there autocorrelation (lag)? What shape does the distribution
+have (histogram)? Is it close to normal (probability plot)?
+
+## MCP Tool
+
+**Tool Name**: `analyze_exploratory_data`
+
+**Signature**:
+```python
+def analyze_exploratory_data(
+    data: list[float],
+    title: str = "Exploratory Data Analysis — 4-Plot",
+) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters**:
+- `data`: One-dimensional sample, at least 4 finite values (below 30 gets an explicit small-sample warning).
+- `title`: Plot title.
+
+**Returns**:
+```json
+{
+  "n": int, "mean": float, "std": float, "min": float, "max": float,
+  "median": float, "skew": float, "kurtosis": float,
+  "lag1_autocorrelation": float,  // null for a constant series
+  "normal_probplot_r": float,     // correlation on the normal paper
+  "small_sample_warning": str,    // or null
+  "file": str,                    // 4-panel PNG in the static dir
+  "message": str
+}
+```
+
+## Reading the output
+
+- Flat run sequence + structureless lag cloud + symmetric histogram + straight probability line → independent, stable, near-normal data.
+- Lag-1 autocorrelation near ±1 → non-random structure; do not fit an IID model without addressing it.
+- Skew/kurtosis plus the histogram shape guide the parametric family shortlist used by `select_life_distribution`.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**MCP Tool**: `analyze_exploratory_data`
+**Implementation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/eda.py`
+**Calculation**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/eda.py`, plots in `plotting.py`
+**Knowledge**: `knowledge-base/nist-eda-exploratory-data-analysis.md` (Ch. 1)
+**Tests**: `backend/tests/test_eda.py`
