+# Knowledge Search Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Hybrid search over reliability engineering documents (handbooks, procedures, notes, standards) combining vector similarity search (ChromaDB) with BM25 keyword matching. Provides comprehensive document retrieval with source citations for knowledge-based queries.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Knowledge search enables the LLM to:
+
+- **Retrieve procedures**: Find reliability testing procedures and standards
+- **Answer factual questions**: Look up who, what, where questions about documents
+- **Cite sources**: Provide traceable references in responses
+- **Context enrichment**: Add domain knowledge to LLM responses
+- **Handbook lookup**: Access company-specific handbooks and guidelines
+
+The system uses local-only embeddings and vector database, ensuring documents never leave the user's machine.
+
+## MCP Tool
+
+**Tool Name**: `search_reliability_knowledge`
+
+**Signature**:
+```python
+def search_reliability_knowledge(query: str, max_results: int = 3) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters**:
+- `query`: Search query in natural language
+- `max_results`: Maximum number of results to return (default: 3)
+
+**Returns**:
+```json
+{
+  "query": str,              // Original query
+  "matches": [               // List of matching chunks
+    {
+      "text": str,           // Chunk text content
+      "source": str,         // Document filename
+      "chunk_number": int,   // Chunk index in document
+      "score": float,        // Combined relevance score
+      "page": int | null,    // Page number (if available)
+      "section": str | null  // Section title (if available)
+    }
+  ],
+  "total_chunks": int,      // Total chunks in knowledge base
+  "embedding_model": str     // Embedding model used
+}
+```
+
+## Implementation
+
+### Tool Registration
+**File**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/server.py`
+
+```python
+@mcp.tool()
+def search_reliability_knowledge(query: str, max_results: int = 3) -> dict[str, Any]:
+    """Hybrid-search local Markdown, text, PDF, Word, and PowerPoint documents."""
+    return _knowledge.search_knowledge(query, max_results)
+```
+
+### Tool Implementation
+**File**: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/knowledge_tool.py`
+
+```python
+def search_knowledge(query: str, max_results: int = 3) -> dict[str, Any]:
+    """Search the reliability knowledge base."""
+    kb = knowledge_base()
+    results = kb.search(query, max_results=max_results)
+    return results
+```
+
+### Core RAG System
+**File**: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+
+Key classes and functions:
+- `GenericKnowledgeBase`: Document ingestion and hybrid search
+- `KnowledgeChunk`: Dataclass for text chunks with metadata
+- `_split_text()`: Paragraph-level chunking with overlap
+- `tokenize_query()`: BM25 tokenization
+- `default_token_count()`: Word counting for chunking
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Document Pipeline
+
+```
+Document Files (.md, .txt, .pdf, .docx, .pptx)
+         ↓
+   Docling Parsing (local, no cloud)
+         ↓
+   Text Extraction
+         ↓
+   Chunking (paragraph-level, overlap)
+         ↓
+   Embedding Generation (Sentence Transformers, local)
+         ↓
+   ChromaDB Storage (vector embeddings)
+         ↓
+   BM25 Index (keyword search)
+```
+
+### Search Pipeline
+
+```
+User Query
+         ↓
+   Query Tokenization (BM25)
+         ↓
+   Query Embedding (Sentence Transformers)
+         ↓
+   Vector Search (ChromaDB similarity)
+         ↓
+   BM25 Search (keyword matching)
+         ↓
+   Score Fusion (weighted combination)
+         ↓
+   Top-K Results
+         ↓
+   Return with citations
+```
+
+### Hybrid Scoring
+
+Combined score = w_vector * vector_score + w_bm25 * bm25_score
+
+Where:
+- `w_vector`: Weight for vector similarity (default: 0.7)
+- `w_bm25`: Weight for BM25 (default: 0.3)
+- Vector search: Semantic similarity (embeddings)
+- BM25: Exact keyword matching
+
+## Document Formats
+
+### Supported Formats
+
+- **Markdown (.md)**: Technical documentation, procedures
+- **Text (.txt)**: Plain text notes
+- **PDF (.pdf)**: Handbooks, standards, reports (parsed with Docling)
+- **Word (.doc, .docx)**: Procedures, specifications (parsed with Docling)
+- **PowerPoint (.ppt, .pptx)**: Presentations, training materials (parsed with Docling)
+
+### Document Processing
+
+1. **File detection**: Scan `knowledge-base/` directory
+2. **Change detection**: SHA256 hash comparison
+3. **Parsing**: Docling extracts text from PDF/Office files
+4. **Chunking**: Split at paragraph boundaries with token limits
+5. **Embedding**: Sentence Transformers generates embeddings
+6. **Indexing**: Store in ChromaDB + BM25 index
+7. **Metadata**: Extract page numbers, sections, source
+
+### Chunking Strategy
+
+- **Paragraph-based**: Split at double newlines
+- **Token limit**: 384 tokens per chunk (default)
+- **Overlap**: 64 tokens between chunks
+- **Preserve context**: Overlap ensures information isn't lost at boundaries
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Procedure Lookup
+
+**User Query**:
+```
+What is the Weibull analysis procedure for censored data?
+```
+
+**LLM Action**:
+```
+Calls search_reliability_knowledge("Weibull analysis procedure censored data", max_results=3)
+```
+
+**Tool Returns**:
+```json
+{
+  "query": "Weibull analysis procedure censored data",
+  "matches": [
+    {
+      "text": "For right-censored data, use Bernard's median rank approximation: MR = (i - 0.3) / (n + 0.4), where i is the failure order number and n is the total sample size including suspensions.",
+      "source": "weibull-procedures.md",
+      "chunk_number": 12,
+      "score": 0.92,
+      "section": "Censored Data Handling"
+    },
+    {
+      "text": "When suspensions are present, rank regression on Y (RRY) is preferred over maximum likelihood estimation for small samples (< 20 failures).",
+      "source": "reliability-handbook.md",
+      "chunk_number": 45,
+      "score": 0.87,
+      "section": "Weibull Methods"
+    }
+  ],
+  "total_chunks": 156,
+  "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
+}
+```
+
+**LLM Response**:
+```
+Based on the reliability procedures:
+
+For right-censored data, use Bernard's median rank approximation:
+```
+MR = (i - 0.3) / (n + 0.4)
+```
+Where:
+- i is the failure order number
+- n is the total sample size including suspensions
+
+[Source: weibull-procedures.md, section "Censored Data Handling"]
+
+When suspensions are present, rank regression on Y (RRY) is preferred over maximum likelihood estimation for small samples (< 20 failures).
+
+[Source: reliability-handbook.md, section "Weibull Methods"]
+```
+
+### Handbook Question
+
+**User Query**:
+```
+Who is responsible for reliability testing in our organization?
+```
+
+**LLM Action**:
+```
+Calls search_reliability_knowledge("responsible reliability testing", max_results=3)
+```
+
+**Tool Returns**:
+```json
+{
+  "query": "responsible reliability testing",
+  "matches": [
+    {
+      "text": "The Reliability Engineering Team, led by Prasanna, is responsible for all reliability testing including HALT, HASS, and life testing.",
+      "source": "org-chart.md",
+      "chunk_number": 3,
+      "score": 0.95
+    }
+  ],
+  "total_chunks": 156,
+  "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
+}
+```
+
+**LLM Response**:
+```
+According to the organizational documentation:
+
+The Reliability Engineering Team, led by Prasanna, is responsible for all reliability testing including HALT, HASS, and life testing.
+
+[Source: org-chart.md]
+```
+
+### Standard Lookup
+
+**User Query**:
+```
+What are the requirements for B10 in our design standards?
+```
+
+**LLM Action**:
+```
+Calls search_reliability_knowledge("B10 requirements design standards", max_results=3)
+```
+
+**Tool Returns**:
+```json
+{
+  "query": "B10 requirements design standards",
+  "matches": [
+    {
+      "text": "Design Standard DS-1234 requires B10 life to be at least 2x the warranty period for all safety-critical components.",
+      "source": "design-standards.md",
+      "chunk_number": 28,
+      "score": 0.89,
+      "section": "Reliability Requirements"
+    }
+  ],
+  "total_chunks": 156,
+  "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
+}
+```
+
+**LLM Response**:
+```
+According to Design Standard DS-1234:
+
+B10 life must be at least 2x the warranty period for all safety-critical components.
+
+[Source: design-standards.md, section "Reliability Requirements"]
+
+For example, if the warranty is 200 hours, B10 must be at least 400 hours for safety-critical parts.
+```
+
+## Knowledge Base Management
+
+### Building the Index
+
+From the backend directory:
+```bash
+uv run python -m src.knowledge.base
+```
+
+This:
+1. Scans `knowledge-base/` directory
+2. Processes new/changed documents
+3. Generates embeddings
+4. Updates ChromaDB and BM25 index
+5. Stores index in `backend/.rag/`
+
+### Downloading Embedding Model
+
+First-time setup:
+```bash
+uv run python -m src.knowledge.base --download-model
+```
+
+Or set `EMBEDDING_LOCAL_FILES_ONLY=true` in `.env` to skip download if model is already cached.
+
+### Adding Documents
+
+1. Drop files into `knowledge-base/` directory
+2. Rebuild index: `uv run python -m src.knowledge.base`
+3. Or upload via chat attachment (auto-ingested)
+
+### Incremental Updates
+
+The system tracks file changes via SHA256 hashes:
+- Only changed files are re-processed
+- New files are added
+- Deleted files are removed from index
+- Fast updates for large knowledge bases
+
+## System Prompt Integration
+
+The reliability domain prompt enforces:
+
+```
+Use search_reliability_knowledge for procedures, handbook questions, and any factual who/what question about people, documents, or local notes. When local knowledge-base context is provided with the question, use it and cite its source.
+```
+
+This ensures the LLM:
+- Uses knowledge search for factual questions
+- Cites sources in responses
+- Doesn't hallucinate information not in documents
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+- `EMBEDDING_MODEL`: Sentence Transformers model (default: all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
+- `EMBEDDING_LOCAL_FILES_ONLY`: Skip model download if true
+- `EMBEDDING_DEVICE`: cpu or cuda (default: cpu)
+
+### Knowledge Base Configuration
+
+Single reliability knowledge base (`backend/src/knowledge/base.py`):
+- `collection`: ChromaDB collection name (`reliability_knowledge`)
+- `knowledge_dir`: Documents directory (`knowledge-base`)
+- `index_dir`: Index directory (`.rag`)
+
+### Chunking Parameters
+
+In `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`:
+- `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS`: 384 tokens per chunk
+- `DEFAULT_OVERLAP_TOKENS`: 64 tokens overlap
+- Customizable per use case
+
+## Performance Characteristics
+
+### Indexing Performance
+
+- **Small documents** (< 10 pages): ~1-2 seconds
+- **Medium documents** (10-50 pages): ~5-10 seconds
+- **Large documents** (50-200 pages): ~20-60 seconds
+- **Embedding generation**: ~100-500ms per chunk
+
+### Search Performance
+
+- **Vector search**: < 100ms for < 10,000 chunks
+- **BM25 search**: < 50ms
+- **Combined query**: < 200ms total
+- **Scales linearly** with chunk count
+
+### Storage Requirements
+
+- **ChromaDB**: ~1KB per chunk (embeddings + metadata)
+- **BM25 index**: ~100 bytes per chunk
+- **Example**: 1000 chunks ≈ 1.1MB index size
+
+## Integration with Other Skills
+
+### Report Generation
+
+The `export_reliability_report` skill can include knowledge citations:
+```python
+export_reliability_report(
+  failure_times=[...],
+  knowledge_query="warranty analysis procedure"
+)
+```
+
+This:
+1. Runs Weibull analysis
+2. Searches knowledge base for the query
+3. Includes citations in the report
+
+### Weibull Analysis
+
+After Weibull fit, the LLM can search for relevant procedures:
+```python
+search_reliability_knowledge("Weibull confidence intervals", max_results=2)
+```
+
+## Limitations
+
+1. **Local only**: No cloud vector DB support (currently)
+2. **File size limit**: Limited by available memory
+3. **No versioning**: No document version tracking
+4. **No OCR**: Scanned PDFs not supported (need text layer)
+5. **No table extraction**: Tables flattened to text
+6. **No real-time updates**: Must rebuild index manually
+7. **Embedding quality**: Depends on model (all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is small but fast)
+
+## Best Practices
+
+### Document Organization
+
+- Use clear filenames (e.g., `weibull-procedures.md` not `doc1.md`)
+- Include section headers in documents
+- Use consistent terminology
+- Keep documents focused on single topics
+- Avoid very long documents (> 200 pages)
+
+### Query Formulation
+
+- Use natural language queries
+- Include specific terms (e.g., "Weibull censored data" not just "Weibull")
+- Ask for procedures or facts separately
+- Use max_results=2-3 for focused answers
+- Use max_results=5-10 for comprehensive searches
+
+### Index Management
+
+- Rebuild index after adding documents
+- Use `--force` flag to force full rebuild
+- Monitor `backend/.rag/` directory size
+- Keep backup of `knowledge-base/` directory
+
+## Security and Privacy
+
+### Local-First Design
+
+- All processing happens locally
+- Documents never leave user's machine
+- No API calls to cloud services
+- Embeddings generated with local model
+- Vector database stored on disk
+
+### Access Control
+
+- Knowledge base access via API only
+- No direct file access from frontend
+- Optional APP_TOKEN for network deployments
+- Per-user knowledge bases in multi-user mode
+
+## Related Skills
+
+- **Weibull Analysis**: Can reference procedures from knowledge base
+- **Report Generation**: Includes knowledge citations in reports
+- **Document Ingestion**: Handles document processing and chunking
+
+## References
+
+- Sentence Transformers: https://www.sbert.net/
+- ChromaDB: https://www.trychroma.com/
+- Docling: https://github.com/DS4SD/docling
+- rank-bm25: https://github.com/dorianbrown/rank_bm25
+
+## Related Files
+
+- Tool: `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/knowledge_tool.py`
+- RAG System: `backend/src/knowledge/base.py`
+- Server: `backend/src/domains/reliability/server.py`
