+# Reliability Growth Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Fits Duane (cumulative MTBF log-log) and Crow-AMSAA / Power-Law NHPP (MLE for shape β and scale λ) to failure times from a single repairable system. Produces growth plots (Duane + Crow-AMSAA mean value), instantaneous MTBF, intensity, Cramer-von Mises GOF, and optional forecast of future MTBF.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Reliability growth analysis tracks whether a system improves (β < 1), stays flat (β = 1), or deteriorates (β > 1) over cumulative test time — essential for demonstrating growth to stakeholders and forecasting when a target MTBF will be reached.
+
+## MCP Tools
+
+### analyze_reliability_growth
+
+```python
+def analyze_reliability_growth(
+    failure_times: list[float],
+    title: str = "Reliability Growth Analysis",
+    time_terminated: float | None = None,
+) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters:** failure_times (≥3, >0, finite), time_terminated (optional truncation time ≥ last failure).
+
+**Returns:** `{ duane: {alpha, K, r_squared, ...}, crow_amsaa: {beta, lambda, intensity_at_T, mtbf_instantaneous, cvm_statistic, cvm_pvalue, ...}, file, message }`
+
+### forecast_growth_mtbf
+
+```python
+def forecast_growth_mtbf(
+    failure_times: list[float],
+    forecast_time: float,
+    time_terminated: float | None = None,
+) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters:** failure_times, forecast_time (>0, finite), time_terminated.
+
+**Returns:** `{ fit, forecast: { forecast_time, forecast_intensity, forecast_mtbf, forecast_cumulative_failures } }`
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `backend/src/domains/reliability/growth_fit.py` — `duane_fit`, `crow_amsaa_fit`, `forecast_crow_amsaa`
+- `backend/src/domains/reliability/growth_plot.py` — `plot_growth_analysis`
+- `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/growth.py` — tool wrappers
+- `backend/tests/test_growth.py`
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- **Duane α > 0** → cumulative MTBF increasing (growth). **α ≈ β−1** for PLP.
+- **Crow-AMSAA β < 1** → failure intensity decreasing (growth); **β = 1** → HPP (no trend); **β > 1** → deterioration.
+- **MTBF_instantaneous = 1 / (λ β T^{β−1})** at last/truncation time T.
+- **CvM GOF** small p ⇒ poor NHPP fit.
