+# Warranty Planning Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+Two deterministic planning calculations built on a fitted (or stated) Weibull
+life distribution: how many field failures to expect inside a warranty
+period, and how to size a zero-failure demonstration test. No values are
+estimated by the LLM; missing inputs are asked for, never assumed.
+
+## MCP Tools
+
+### forecast_warranty_failures
+
+```python
+def forecast_warranty_failures(
+    beta: float, eta: float, warranty_time: float, population: int,
+    confidence: float = 0.90, units: str = "hours",
+) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters:** fitted beta/eta (>0, finite), warranty_time (>0, same units
+as eta), population (positive whole number), confidence in (0, 1), units.
+
+**Returns:** `{ reliability_at_warranty, failure_probability_by_warranty,
+expected_failures, failure_count_interval, method, assumptions, ... }`
+
+Each unit fails by warranty_time with probability `F(t) = 1 - exp(-(t/eta)^beta)`;
+the count is Binomial(population, F), and the interval is its central
+binomial interval. Fit uncertainty in beta/eta is stated as not propagated.
+
+### plan_demonstration_test
+
+```python
+def plan_demonstration_test(
+    target_reliability: float, confidence: float, assumed_beta: float,
+    mission_time: float, sample_size: int | None = None,
+    test_duration: float | None = None, units: str = "hours",
+) -> dict[str, Any]
+```
+
+**Parameters:** target reliability and confidence in (0, 1), assumed
+(known) Weibull beta, mission_time, and exactly one of sample_size /
+test_duration.
+
+**Returns:** `{ mode, sample_size, test_duration, achieved_confidence,
+zero_failures_allowed, method, assumptions, ... }`
+
+Solves the success-run relation `C = 1 - R^(n*(t/mission_time)^beta)` for
+the unknown. Sample sizes are rounded up; achieved confidence is reported.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `backend/src/domains/reliability/planning.py` — `warranty_failure_forecast`, `demonstration_test_plan`
+- `backend/src/domains/reliability/tools/planning.py` — tool wrappers
+- `backend/tests/test_planning.py`
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- Expected warranty failures scale linearly with population at fixed F(t);
+  widen the interval by raising `confidence`.
+- A demonstration plan proves only the stated claim (reliability >= R at the
+  mission time, at the stated confidence, under the assumed beta) and only
+  if the test finishes with zero failures.
