+
+## Rich Rendering
+
+### Markdown Rendering
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx`
+
+```typescript
+<ReactMarkdown
+  remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}
+  rehypePlugins={[rehypeSanitize]}
+  components={{
+    // Custom components for code blocks, tables, etc.
+  }}
+>
+  {content}
+</ReactMarkdown>
+```
+
+**Features**:
+- GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM)
+- HTML sanitization (security)
+- Code blocks with syntax highlighting
+- Tables
+- Task lists
+- Strikethrough
+
+### KaTeX Integration
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/components/MessageItem.tsx`
+
+```tsx
+<ReactMarkdown
+  remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm, remarkMath]}
+  rehypePlugins={[
+    [rehypeSanitize, katexSanitizeSchema],
+    [rehypeKatex, { output: 'html', throwOnError: false, strict: false }],
+  ]}
+>
+  {content}
+</ReactMarkdown>
+```
+
+**Rendering rules**:
+- Declarative KaTeX (`remark-math` + `rehype-katex`), not MathJax typesetting.
+- Sanitize runs **before** KaTeX: KaTeX HTML positions sub/superscripts and
+  fractions with inline styles, which a later sanitize pass would strip and
+  collapse (e.g. `$B_{10}$` stacking its `10` below the `B`). Raw-HTML styles
+  from the message source are still neutralized by the sanitize pass.
+- Standard LaTeX notation: `$B_{10}$`, `$\beta$`, `$\eta$` (legacy `\sb{}`
+  still maps to a subscript for old messages; new output must not use it).
+
+### Math Repair
+
+**Files**: `frontend/src/utils/mathMarkdown.ts`, `backend/src/common/markdown_math.py`
+(mirrored logic — keep both in sync)
+
+```typescript
+export function patchMarkdownMath(text: string): string {
+  // Normalize math delimiters to $...$ / $$...$$, balance braces,
+  // escape bare %, and move [source] citations out of math delimiters.
+}
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Repair common LLM TeX mistakes (unclosed delimiters, unbalanced
+braces, citations glued inside `$...$`) before Markdown/KaTeX rendering, so
+formulas render instead of breaking.
+
+## Message Actions
+
+### Copy
+
+**Implementation**: Clipboard API
+
+```typescript
+navigator.clipboard.writeText(content);
+```
+
+### Edit and Resend
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks edit on message
+2. Message content loaded into composer
+3. User modifies and sends
+3. Original message replaced with new message
+4. LLM regenerates response
+
+### Regenerate
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks regenerate on assistant message
+2. Last user message resent to LLM
+3. New response generated
+4. Old assistant message replaced
+
+### Delete
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks delete on message
+2. Message removed from session
+3. If session empty, session deleted
+
+## Image Rendering
+
+### Plot Images
+
+**Flow**:
+1. Backend generates plot (e.g., `weibull_abc123.png`)
+2. Backend returns `image` event with URL
+3. Frontend displays image in message
+4. Image served from `/static/` directory
