+# Model Picker Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+LLM provider selection and configuration interface supporting multiple OpenAI-compatible endpoints. Enables users to switch between local LLM providers (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp) and cloud providers (OpenAI, custom) with runtime configuration and connection testing.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Model picker enables:
+
+- **Provider selection**: Choose from multiple LLM providers
+- **Runtime configuration**: Change provider without restarting backend
+- **Connection testing**: Test LLM endpoint before using
+- **Model listing**: Fetch available models from endpoint
+- **API key management**: Secure API key input (not persisted in localStorage)
+- **Provider presets**: Pre-configured defaults for common providers
+
+## Supported Providers
+
+### Local Providers
+
+**Ollama**
+- Default URL: `http://localhost:11434`
+- Models API: `/api/tags`
+- Use case: Local inference, privacy
+
+**LM Studio**
+- Default URL: `http://localhost:1234`
+- Models API: `/v1/models`
+- Use case: Local inference, GUI
+
+**llama.cpp**
+- Default URL: `http://localhost:8080`
+- Models API: `/v1/models`
+- Use case: Local inference, CPU/GPU
+
+**Unsloth**
+- Default URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8888`
+- Models API: `/v1/models`
+- Use case: Local inference, fine-tuning
+
+**LiteRT-LM**
+- Default URL: `http://localhost:9379`
+- Models API: `/v1/models`
+- Use case: Mobile/on-device inference
+
+### Cloud Providers
+
+**OpenAI**
+- Default URL: `https://api.openai.com/v1`
+- Models API: `/v1/models`
+- Use case: Cloud inference, GPT models
+
+**Custom**
+- User-specified URL
+- Models API: `/v1/models` (OpenAI-compatible)
+- Use case: Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
+
+## Implementation
+
+### Component
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/components/ModelPicker.tsx`
+
+```typescript
+export function ModelPicker({
+  provider,
+  baseUrl,
+  apiKey,
+  model,
+  onProviderChange,
+  onBaseUrlChange,
+  onApiKeyChange,
+  onModelChange,
+  onTest
+}: ModelPickerProps) {
+  // Provider dropdown with presets
+  // Base URL input with normalization
+  // API key input (write-only)
+  // Model dropdown with refresh
+  // Test connection button
+}
+```
+
+### Provider Presets
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/types/llm.ts`
+
+```typescript
+export const PROVIDER_DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = {
+  ollama: 'http://localhost:11434',
+  lmstudio: 'http://localhost:1234',
+  llamacpp: 'http://localhost:8080',
+  unsloth: 'http://127.0.0.1:8888',
+  openai: 'https://api.openai.com/v1',
+  litert: 'http://localhost:9379',
+  custom: '',
+};
+```
+
+### Backend Integration
+
+**API Endpoints**:
+- `GET /api/models` - List available models
+- `GET /api/llm/config` - Get current LLM configuration
+- `PUT /api/llm/config` - Save LLM configuration
+- `POST /api/llm/test` - Test LLM connection
+
+**Backend Service**:
+**File**: `frontend/src/services/browser/httpApi.ts`
+
+```typescript
+listModels: (signal?: AbortSignal) => req<LlmModelsResponse>('/api/models', { signal }),
+getLlmConfig: (signal?: AbortSignal) => req<LlmConfig>('/api/llm/config', { signal }),
+saveLlmConfig: (update: LlmConfigUpdate, signal?: AbortSignal) =>
+  req<LlmConfig>('/api/llm/config', {
+    method: 'PUT',
+    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
+    body: JSON.stringify(update),
+    signal,
+  }),
+testLlmConfig: (update: LlmConfigUpdate, signal?: AbortSignal) =>
+  req<LlmTestResult>('/api/llm/test', {
+    method: 'POST',
+    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
+    body: JSON.stringify(update),
+    signal,
+  }),
+```
+
+## URL Normalization
+
+### Backend Normalization
+
+**File**: `backend/src/host/app.py`
+
+```python
+def normalize_base_url(raw: str | None) -> str:
+    """Reduce a pasted endpoint URL to its root (no doubled /v1/... segments)."""
+    base = (raw or "").strip().rstrip("/")
+    lowered = base.lower()
+    for suffix in _KNOWN_ENDPOINT_SUFFIXES:
+        if lowered.endswith(suffix) and len(base) > len(suffix):
+            base = base[: -len(suffix)].rstrip("/")
+            break
+    return base
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Users often paste full URLs like `http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions`. Normalization extracts the root: `http://localhost:11434`.
+
+### OpenAI API Base
+
+```python
+def openai_api_base(base: str) -> str:
+    """Return the OpenAI-compatible root, guaranteeing exactly one /v1."""
+    base = (base or "").strip().rstrip("/")
+    if re.search(r"/v1$", base, re.IGNORECASE):
+        return base
+    return f"{base}/v1"
+```
+
+## Model Listing
+
+### Ollama Models
+
+**Special Case**: Ollama uses `/api/tags` instead of `/v1/models`
+
+**Backend Handling**:
+```python
+# In app.py
+if provider == "ollama":
+    models_url = f"{base}/api/tags"
+else:
+    models_url = f"{base}/v1/models"
+```
+
+**Response Format**:
+```json
+{
+  "models": [
+    {"name": "llama3.1:8b", "size": 4877051392},
+    {"name": "llama3.1:70b", "size": 40178350848}
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Standard OpenAI Format
+
+**Response Format**:
+```json
+{
+  "object": "list",
+  "data": [
+    {"id": "gpt-4", "object": "model"},
+    {"id": "gpt-3.5-turbo", "object": "model"}
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Connection Testing
+
+### Test Endpoint
+
+**Request**:
+```http
+POST /api/llm/test
+Content-Type: application/json
+
+{
+  "provider": "ollama",
+  "baseUrl": "http://localhost:11434",
+  "apiKey": "",
+  "model": "llama3.1:8b"
+}
